sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant DS as Data Scientist
    participant CI as Rater repo CI
    participant H as Backtest harness (rater code as a library)
    participant API as Internal API
    participant L as AWS Lambda
    participant OI as Ops interface (business approver)

    DS->>H: run locally first (same CLI as CI)
    DS->>CI: pull request (rules, table or module change)
    CI->>CI: unit tests + generate manifest from the input declaration
    CI->>API: fetch live program versions that would adopt this rater
    CI->>CI: compatibility report: which programs can adopt as-is, which need changes (informational, adoption is a separate publish)
    CI->>H: replay set + rating test cases, previous rater vs this change
    H-->>CI: impact report (changed %, top movers, new declines, errors, spreadsheet diffs to the cent)
    CI-->>DS: report posted on the PR
    alt refactor (no intended price change) and any premium differs
        CI-->>DS: fail
    end
    DS->>CI: merge after review
    CI->>L: publish new numbered Lambda version
    CI->>API: register rating_engine_version (endpoint = numbered version, manifest, code_ref)
    API->>API: carry question definitions forward by key (new rows, old untouched), flag new or changed ones for wording
    Note over API: registered, charges nobody yet
    DS->>OI: draft base program version pinning the new rater
    OI->>H: automatic backtest of the base program on the new rater
    OI->>OI: business approver signs off on the report (the green light)
    OI->>API: publish on effective date, rebase drafts created for partner programs
